title: 'statement-store: split the v2 inbound statement slots by peer role'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    With the v2 DHT path on, the statement set reserves only the peers that steering picks, every
    other peer holds an inbound slot and the protocol controller dials no peer of its own. The set
    gets the node's light allowance on top of its inbound slots and the handler splits them by
    role, so a light peer is admitted while the full slots are taken.
    `StatementHandlerPrototype::new` takes the network configuration as a new argument.
crates:
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: major
